# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Contractor OS — environment variable template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is git-ignored and
# MUST NEVER be committed (see SECURITY note below).
#
# In production (Vercel / your host), set these as environment variables in the
# hosting provider's dashboard — do not rely on a committed .env file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database — Neon PostgreSQL is the canonical persistence layer (INVARIANT 10).
# DATABASE_URL uses the pooled connection (PgBouncer transaction mode) for
# regular queries. DIRECT_DATABASE_URL uses the direct connection for
# interactive transactions ($transaction with callback).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&connect_timeout=15
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require

# NextAuth.js — generate a strong secret with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=replace-with-openssl-rand-base64-32
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# z-ai-web-dev-sdk (AI features — advisory only; AI never commits a price).
ZAI_BASE_URL=https://internal-api.z.ai/v1
ZAI_API_KEY=replace-with-your-zai-api-key
ZAI_CHAT_ID=replace-with-your-zai-chat-id
ZAI_TOKEN=replace-with-your-zai-token
ZAI_USER_ID=replace-with-your-zai-user-id

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY — READ THIS
#
# A previous version of this repository committed a real .env containing live
# credentials to git history. Even though .env is now untracked and .gitignore
# covers it, THE OLD SECRETS REMAIN IN GIT HISTORY and must be treated as
# COMPROMISED. Rotating the file out of tracking does NOT rotate the secrets.
#
# If you are the operator of this repository, perform ALL of the following
# before treating the repository as security-clean:
#
#   1. Neon PostgreSQL — rotate the database password (or, preferably, create
#      a fresh Neon project / branch and re-point DATABASE_URL /
#      DIRECT_DATABASE_URL). The old connection strings in history are dead.
#   2. NEXTAUTH_SECRET — generate a new secret (openssl rand -base64 32) and
#      update it in every environment (local .env, Vercel, CI). Rotating this
#      invalidates all existing JWT sessions (users must sign in again) — that
#      is expected and acceptable.
#   3. Z.ai credentials — rotate/revoke ZAI_API_KEY and ZAI_TOKEN in the Z.ai
#      console. Reissue ZAI_CHAT_ID / ZAI_USER_ID if those are sensitive in
#      your tenant.
#   4. Update the rotated secrets in the Vercel project dashboard (and any CI
#      environment) — never re-commit them to the repo.
#   5. (Optional but recommended) Purge .env from git history using
#      `git filter-repo` or BFG Repo-Cleaner, then force-push. This is not a
#      substitute for rotation — anyone who already cloned/forked the repo
#      still has the old secrets — but it stops future exposure. Coordinate
#      with all collaborators before force-pushing.
#
# Going forward, the test loader (tests/setup.ts) requires TEST_DATABASE_URL
# in CI (mandatory, no .env fallback) so destructive integration tests target
# a dedicated test database, never the application database.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
